  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1216 PM MDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nThe upper high is forecast to remain over the southeast US, while\na west coast trough/low meanders around the Pacific NW and Great \nBasin through the end of the week. This setup will allow a Monsoon\nmoisture plume to stand up over the region, resulting in a \ncontinued uptrend in PWATs through mid week and then remaining \nelevated through at least Friday. PWATs are forecast to challenge \ndaily records each day this week, with the Tuesday through \nThursday period being the peak. The result will be a wet period \nwith good chances for showers and storms and the potential for \nlocally heavy rainfall and flash flooding. The WPC shows much of \nour area in a slight risk for excessive rainfall on Wednesday and \nThursday, which look to be the most active days. With \nincreasingly wet antecedent conditions from mid through late \nweek, there is a good chances that Flash Flood Watches will be \nrequired both on and off area burn scars. Daytime temperatures \nwill trend down through the week thanks to added cloud cover and \nrain- cooling, with highs forecast to be at or below average most \nareas from Wednesday onward.",
